No, they're not.  In fact, any comestibles other than fruit/veggies,
tins, eggs, cream pies or rotten, acidic, poisonous or vegan corpses
will work for taming cats and dogs.  Horses can be tamed with fruit or
veggies (including user-defined fruit) or with vegan corpses, provided
they're not rotten, acidic or poisonous.

Spare lizard corpses can be particularly handy for taming cats and
dogs since they never rot, weigh little and since you have other
reasons to collect and carry them anyway.  (Of course, meatballs are
even more convenient for healers.)  Similarly, lichen corpses can be
useful for taming horses.

In fact, throwing *any* comestible (other than eggs or cream pies,
which go splat) at a domestic animal will at least make it peaceful.
Yes, this works even with cockatrice corpses(!).  This can be worth
remembering if you're, say, about to get kicked to death by a
warhorse: even a rotten corpse or a random tin will work to pacify it.

(I do realize you probably know much of this, and in any case already
solved the original problem.  But I figure someone may find it useful,
so I might as well post it all now that I've taken the time to peek at
the source.)

